"""The OpenSSL names the native _ssl and _hashlib ports use, as the C modules
they replace named them: one entry per source line that names one, in source
order, as (whether the line is an #if condition, the OpenSSL-prefixed names on
it, the identifiers on it not seen on an earlier line). gen_openssl.jac reads
the names, and expands the identifiers that are function-like OpenSSL macros.
Taken once from those C modules; see jac/jaclang/runtime/python/LICENSE.cpython.
"""

